# May 2026. For some reason, when rendering from within Rstudio, it thinks that the current
# working directory is ~/home/gianluca and so it creates a site_libs folder under it every
# time that a page is rendered. This doesn't happen when rendering from terminal using quarto
# directly, though. The following command in the .Rprofile does fix the issue.
options(htmlwidgets.dir = "public/site_libs")
